        "discrepancy": "Section 3 is internally inconsistent and conflicts with the project record: it declares actual capacitance 680 uF, but its t_99.9 calculation still uses 750 uF. The 750 uF calculation reproduces at 2.435 s; for 680 uF the checker recomputes 2.2077 s, and 2.5 s reaches 99.96%. Separately, an earlier purchasing decision adds 140 uF and states the HV bus is 820 uF; at 820 uF, 2.5 s reaches only 99.848% and does not meet the 99.9% check. Section 4 also prints 6.91 s for 2 mF, while the checker recomputes 6.4933 s.",
        "why_it_matters": "The review cannot be signed against one settled bus capacitance. The timer margin and pass/fail result depend on whether 680 uF or the documented 820 uF configuration is authoritative. The 2 mF worked example is numerically wrong even though it is separate from the bus decision.",
